1	// THE FIVE-STAGE SPECIALIST PIPELINE over a multi-file work-unit DAG: the orchestrator.
2	//
3	//   Stage 1  plan          work_units (work-units.mjs) — validated here, authored upstream by the planner
4	//   Stage 2  dispatch      dispatcher specialist + frozen rubric; controller locks, waves, worktrees (dispatch.mjs)
5	//   Stage 3  implement     one specialist per unit in its own worktree, behind the write jail (implement.mjs)
6	//   Stage 4  subagents     the per-unit A2A leaf shim on a Unix socket (a2a-shim.mjs), reached by the agent through
7	//                          the stdio MCP relay a2a-mcp-server.mjs
8	//   Stage 5  review        pinned to the Stage 2 model; ground truth from verify_cmd; the ladder (review.mjs)
9	//
10	// Inputs: runPipeline({repo, base, plan, seats, turns, limits, dir, signal, planner?, run_id?, sameModel?, checkpoints?}).
11	// Seats and turns are INJECTED: this module imports no routing table, no vendor SDK and calls no provider.
12	// Outputs: the run record (schema pantheon.pipeline/v1), returned and written INCREMENTALLY to <dir>/pipeline.json
13	// after every step, so a crash leaves a truthful record of what had happened.
14	//
15	// The controller here is code ({vendor: "controller"}): it decides what is dispatched, kept, merged and skipped.
16	//
17	// PER-UNIT CONTROL DIRECTORY. <dir>/control/<unit_id>/ (mode 0700) is created by the controller for every active
18	// unit, OUTSIDE its worktree, and handed to the implementer turn as `control_dir`. The unit's A2A shim listens on
19	// <control_dir>/a2a.sock; when that path is over the Unix socket-path bound (SOCKET_PATH_MAX), on a short path in a
20	// fresh controller-owned directory under os.tmpdir() instead. The path used is recorded (units[id].a2a.socket) and
21	// the socket file (and a fallback directory) removed when the unit ends.
22	//
23	// THE IMPLEMENTER LANE FAILOVER LADDER. A turn that throws code "lane_failure" (kind timeout | exit | stream | spawn)
24	// is retried on THE SAME lane at most once, then the unit steps down to the next rung of its implementer ladder
25	// (seats.implementer(unit).ladder); a turn that throws code "quota_exhausted" (the transport's own quota failover
26	// already failed) steps down at once. Lane failures spend no revision (max_revisions counts Stage 5 rejections and
27	// refused attempts only) but every call is charged to max_provider_calls. Each failover is an `escalations[]` entry
28	// of kind "lane_failover"; each failed call is in attempts[].lane_failures [{vendor, model, level, kind, cause, why,
29	// retry (true: this call was the same-lane retry), next}]. With no rung left the unit ends blocked, code
30	// LANE_LADDER_EXHAUSTED. A later rejection escalates the thinking level from the rung failover left it on.
31	//
32	// CHECKPOINTS (checkpoint.mjs). With `checkpoints: {dir}` (a directory that persists across runs of one item),
33	// every unit approved by Stage 5 is written there; a later run re-verifies a unit's checkpoint (digest, upstream
34	// trees, and the patch applied on the freshly bound base yielding the recorded tree) and, if it holds, takes the
35	// unit as approved with `resumed: true` and no provider call. A checkpoint that does not hold is recorded as
36	// `checkpoint_rejected` and the unit runs normally.
37	//
38	// Must never: merge a unit that was not approved against a passing verify_cmd; run a unit whose upstream did not
39	// merge; exceed an injected limit; let an injected function mutate the frozen unit; block the event loop on git.
