1	// The real stage executors of the governed lifecycle (scheduler.mjs calls them): plan -> implement -> review ->
2	// validate -> outcome, each over Pantheon's existing machinery rather than a rebuilt copy of it.
3	//
4	//   plan       evaluation and planning. A planner seat (selectSeat role planner) writes a SUBSTANTIVE plan
5	//              document (ophanim.plan/v1), checked deterministically (a one-line title is refused); the plan is
6	//              committed on its own ref and reviewed by a coordinated three-lab cycle (reviewCycle) on labs that did
7	//              not write it; blocking findings are answered by a revision that is re-reviewed. Only an exact,
8	//              approved plan version writes (or, re-validated, keeps byte-identical) tickets/<item>.json.
9	//   implement  the approved ticket through runOpenItem (acceptance and in-run review), the shipped bytes committed
10	//              on pantheon/<item> (commitShipped). Review capacity is checked before any work call.
11	//              UNDER THE `fit` PROFILE, with a plan that carries `work_units`: the five-stage specialist pipeline
12	//              (pantheon/src/pipeline runPipeline: dispatcher -> implementer in a per-unit worktree -> subagents ->
13	//              pinned reviewer -> integration), its integrated tree committed on pantheon/<item> the same way.
14	//              `argo` and `legacy` keep the per-file runOpenItem path, unchanged.
15	//   review     the coordinated three-lab cycle review of base..commit (reviewCycle), independent of every recorded
16	//              contribution (changeScope plus the plan's and the critiques'). n is 3 and is never lowered; a short
17	//              pool or a failed reviewer is `pending`, the work and the open cycle kept (resumed, never reopened).
18	//   validate   the plan's acceptance commands and a regression command in a CLEAN checkout of the exact commit, then
19	//              an independent validator's judgment against the ORIGINAL requirement: accept, implementation_defect
20	//              (returned to implement) or plan_defect (returned to plan). Green tests alone never pass.
21	//   outcome    the UNSIGNED status proposal (proposeFromBundle) bound to the item, ticket and reviewed, validated
22	//              commit. Never signed: the owner applies it.
23	//
24	// Inputs: {repo, makeClientFor (the work seats), turn (single-turn seats: planner, reviewers, validator), n = 3,
25	// statusRoot, stateDir, scouts, revisions, seating (the configured reviewer pool, default Pantheon's), facts (its seat facts;
26	// tests inject a synthetic pool with both), pipelineLimits (overrides of the pipeline's DEFAULT_LIMITS under `fit`; the
27	// provider-call bound is the stage budget, or a lower max_provider_calls given here), meteredFailover (default true; false:
28	// a Gemini lane's quota refusal in the pipeline is never answered by the metered Gemini API, pipeline/turns.mjs)}. Every stage
29	// stays within ctx.budget.provider_calls; a failed or refused call is counted. Vendor SDKs stay at the edge.
