42	 * the two ways a turn can be served; it imports no SDK.
43	 *
44	 *   a seat naming a metered Gemini API id that has an Antigravity lane  -> that lane first (at the seat's effort;
45	 *                                                                          `high` when it carries none)
46	 *   a seat naming a lane                                                -> that lane
47	 *   anything else                                                       -> `api`, unchanged
48	 *
49	 * The metered API answers ONLY when the lane attempt was refused for quota (HTTP 429 / quota exhausted, as
50	 * classifyFailure classifies it), and the answer then says so (`quota_failover`). Any other lane failure is thrown as
